build/runtime_qwen21-nvfp4-conditioning.patch
=============================================

Attribution
-----------
Source: BennyDaBall/Qwen-Image-2.1-NVFP4 (Hugging Face model repository)
        runtime/qwen21-nvfp4-conditioning.patch
        https://huggingface.co/BennyDaBall/Qwen-Image-2.1-NVFP4
Upstream revision: 1a38d44a3a2f35cb0b543a25b04da0a963e7b5e6
Upstream documentation: runtime/README.md in the same repository.
Bundled copy SHA-256 (as vendored here):
  2c13ec9046ffa720484c569acce153f4759da47e9bc008af56d68d583854e2fa

What the patch changes
----------------------
Qwen Image 2.1 NVFP4 conditioning: it detects NVFP4 checkpoint metadata in the
text-encoder state dict, converts the completed multimodal embeddings to BF16 on
GPUs with NVFP4 compute support, and runs the encoder forward pass inside
ComfyUI's existing quantized-matmul context. BF16 and INT8 checkpoints keep the
original code path unchanged; vision preprocessing and the unnormalized final
hidden state contract are preserved.

Tested base: 99073836d45f66053c45ba8564984e6def9cebba (an independent patch, not
an upstream ComfyUI release). The Dockerfile applies it against the pinned
ComfyUI checkout with ``git apply --check`` followed by ``git apply``, so a
mismatch fails the build instead of silently degrading.

